.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Kenichi Fukui, Teijiro Yonezawa and Haruo Shingu (1952) proposed that an aromatic hydrocarbon&#x27;s site of electrophilic substitution is set by one orbital alone, the highest occupied molecular orbital: the attacking electrophile goes where the HOMO density 2c_r^2 is largest. For naphthalene the Huckel HOMO has coefficient 0.425 on the alpha carbons (1, 4, 5, 8), 0.263 on the beta carbons (2, 3, 6, 7), and zero on the bridgeheads, so frontier_electron_density predicts alpha substitution, which is what nitration and halogenation mostly give.">

